WEBVTT

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.350
Peruse at your leisure.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.850
Security sure is tight in
the Forbidden Collection.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.020
This is incredible!

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:41.290
None of this information was
available in the main library.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.710
Are you thinking about murdering someone?

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.420
S-Ser Drewes! When did you get here?!

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.380
Wouldn't <i>you </i>like to know!

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.720
Those are poisonous plants, correct?

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:03.100
Well, I figured that in small amounts,
they could be used in medicines.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.060
I'm telling the truth!

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.820
I suppose we can leave it at that.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.440
I swear it's the truth!

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.700
I thought I might be able to use them
to make even stronger potions.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.950
Uh-huh.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.250
In any case, I'm looking for herbs that
<i>aren't </i>typically used in potion-making,

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.040
because maybe they'll open
the door to new possibilities.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.380
New possibilities, you say?

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:39.090
Did you know that plants possess
a small amount of magic within them?

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.350
Wait, really?

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:47.900
All living things possess
some quantity of magic.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.560
I didn't know that.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.400
Most do not. I only learned of it
through my own research.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.740
I hypothesize the reason your
potions are especially effective

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:05.200
is because the magic you imbue into the
potion is different from other casters'.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.750
As such, if you were to imbue the herbs
themselves with your magic power...

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.340
You can do that?!

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.380
Who knows?

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.180
But <i>you </i>might be able to, Lady Sei...

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:05.030
Awakening

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.450
It didn't work.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.160
It's still just water, then?

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.540
I guess because water's the base for
the potion, you can't imbue it with magic.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:20.260
I'll admit, trying to imbue
the water we use for the garden

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.220
is a pretty interesting idea.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:29.390
In the video games in my homeworld,
they had this thing called "holy water."

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:33.230
Hey, does holy water exist in this world?

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.690
"Holey" water?

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.570
It's like... water with magic in it.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.110
Never heard of anything like that.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.700
How did they make holy water again?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.390
Crafting

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.390
Herbs

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.390
Blessing

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.390
Holy Water

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.290
A <i>blessing</i>?

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.330
Yes.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.170
So, uh, in my world, there's a special
kind of water called "holy water."

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.460
All right.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:07.010
It can purify areas, or take out
undead monsters, things like that.

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.220
I see.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:13.020
And to make holy water,
you need to "bless" it.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.900
I've never heard of anything of the sort.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.400
Yeah, figured.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.020
But it's interesting in concept.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:26.240
And fascinating how it's particularly
effective against one type of monster.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:31.910
Oh, in my world, we didn't have magic,
so those "facts" are just fantasy.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.660
That matters not.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.080
Still, one wonders...

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:42.380
A thought comes to mind, but please,
don't dwell upon it too deeply.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.880
All right.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:49.090
I do know of a type of magic that is
effective against <i>all </i>types of monsters.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:57.560
All I know of it is that it exists, and
nothing of its abilities or potency.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.320
But we do have records of casters
who knew how to use it.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.570
What is it?

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:08.070
This type of magic is
called "Saintly conjury."

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:12.450
Do you know how the Saints
used this "conjury"?

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.330
Jesus.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:23.500
I have two questions about
that, if you don't mind.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.170
By all means, please.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:28.300
First, what can Saintly conjury <i>do</i>?

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:32.260
It purifies miasma and destroys
the monsters born of it.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.850
Second, what is it I'm trying to do?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:41.770
Imbue plants with your magic power
to create more powerful potions, yes?

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:45.940
It doesn't sound like
this could help with that.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:50.860
Indeed. That is why I told you
not to think <i>too </i>deeply upon it.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.280
Come <i>on</i>.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.130
Working late, I see.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.880
Ser Director!

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.590
I saw you casting spells out in
the garden. Is this somehow related?

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:11.340
I was hoping you wouldn't notice that.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.760
How could I miss it when
you're casting up a storm?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.350
Did it help you learn anything new?

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.640
Somewhat.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:25.150
I learned that magic can
somehow affect plants.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:30.110
Really? So holy-affinity magic
<i>also </i>works on plants, then?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.160
What do you mean, "also"?

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:38.370
Well, we know that earth- and
water-affinity magic can affect plants.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.370
They can?

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:45.670
Why did you try to cast
holy-affinity magic out there?

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:46.840
Well...

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.010
I think I get it now.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:58.020
So you're trying to imbue
the plants with magic?

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.520
Yes, but it didn't quite
work out as I wanted.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:05.150
The only thing I haven't tried is
this "Saintly conjury" I heard of,

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.820
but nobody knows anything about it.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.820
Saintly conjury, you say?

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.440
You've heard of it?

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:13.780
Only stories and rumors.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.450
I haven't read any detailed
accounts of its use.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:17.740
I thought so.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:26.170
Perhaps it's not the type of magic the
casters thought to record for posterity.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:30.090
The names and effects of the spells
we can cast are the same,

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.720
no matter the ability or
potential of the caster.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:34.680
Right.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:38.390
So we find merit in preserving that
information in tomes and grimoires

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:41.480
to communicate it to other users of magic.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:45.980
But this "Saintly conjury" can only be
used by a small handful of casters.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:50.070
Its use may be too specific--
destroying monsters--

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:55.240
and its method of casting may
have differed between Saints.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.950
I see.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:09:01.330
Though I suppose all this doesn't
teach you any more about it.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.460
I'm sorry I can't be of more help.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.000
No, don't be.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:09.420
Don't push yourself too hard, all right?

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.260
I won't, thank you!

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.780
It's getting so cold at night now.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:42.410
I can see so many more
stars in this world.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:49.420
I feel like it's gotten harder and harder
to remember my world lately.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.590
Did I care that little about it?

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.640
Still...

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:02.560
This world is so much warmer
than the one I left,

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.560
and so many wonderful people
have lent me a helping hand.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:11.900
I wish I could do something...

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.360
...to help <i>them</i>, too.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:16.360
Huh?

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.160
Wh-What the...

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.740
What's going on?!

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:03.080
Sei...

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.160
I don't know, either!

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.970
I see you're hard at work, as always.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:30.690
Two Knightly Orders need lots
of potions, so, you know.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:36.070
I feel terrible, seeing as you're the
only one who can craft these potions.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:40.780
It's all right. I only wish we'd been
able to harvest more of those herbs.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:49.250
Especially since anyone could create
your more effective potions with them.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:54.420
I was so excited that my
experiment was a success,

00:11:54.420 --> 00:12:00.550
but I still haven't been able to cast that
spell again, though I've been trying.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.470
You are full of mysteries, aren't you?

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.300
I'm so sorry.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:08.520
Please, <i>I'm </i>sorry we
can't be of more help.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.140
Especially today.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:16.610
A messenger came from the Palace today.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:20.530
They're requesting a healer to support
them on their next expedition.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.360
They want you to help?

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.700
Don't play dumb. They're after <i>you</i>.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:27.330
Sorry, bad joke. I know.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:32.080
You sure are calm. I expected you
to be a little more upset about the it.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.960
I mean, I can't say I'm too excited...

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:42.420
...but I want to do whatever I can

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:45.300
to make sure nothing like
that happens ever again.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:47.100
I see.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.760
Plus...

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:53.270
...there are probably some herbs in the
Western Woods I've never seen before!

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:56.190
Well, <i>I'd </i>say you're pretty excited about
the prospect of going along.

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:57.360
Was it that obvious?

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.160
Perfect!

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:17.580
Oh, good morning, Jude.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:19.550
Hey, Sei! Morning.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:26.340
Huh? You're here too, Ser Director?
Why are you up so early?

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.890
Are you really asking us that?

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.430
We're here to see you off.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:31.430
What?!

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:33.730
You can be so dense.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:38.190
You're headed off to the Western Woods,
right? Those're dangerous parts.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.650
She'll be all right.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:40.770
Huh?

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:45.400
You don't need to worry.
I'll be by your side the entire time.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:50.280
Wh-What are you doing here
this early, Commander Hawke?

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.290
I've come to accompany you.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:54.080
Th-Thank you for thinking of me!

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.680
Stay safe out there!

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.480
Good morning, Lady Sei!

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.070
T-To what do I owe this honor?

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:28.610
Nothing, I just thought I'd keep
you company in your carriage.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:29.450
All right.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.200
Now, how did you successfully
accomplish the cast?

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.290
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:39.960
Goodness, you can be <i>such </i>a tease.
You know what I'm talking about.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.630
The conjury.

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:43.840
Wh-Who told you about that?!

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.880
Wouldn't <i>you </i>like to know!

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.420
But that's hardly important.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:49.760
What did you need to do
to achieve the cast?!

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:54.390
I-I'm not sure. All of the sudden, there
were these golden lights around me...

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.640
You <i>must </i>tell me everything!

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.190
Perhaps one of the conditions
for utilizing the Saint's conjury

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.690
is a lack of awareness
that the conjury is being cast!

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:06.190
Can you give me any more details?

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:08.900
About how much magic power did you use?
How large was the area of effect?

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:11.200
How long did it last?
How did it affect you physically?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.830
You <i>must </i>show me how you do it!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:22.250
H-Hold on a minute! I haven't been
able to do it since that one time!

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.340
What?

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:28.010
So I don't know if what I did was really
the Saint's conjury we talked about.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.760
Is that so...

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.850
But I'm trying to do it again,

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:37.890
so once I figure it out,
I'll be sure to show you.

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:39.310
I expect you to keep that promise.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:51.410
Sei, how was your carriage ride?

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:56.240
Good, thank you! Once I started talking
to Ser Drewes, time just flew by.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.330
I'm glad to hear that.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.660
Besides, if I'm achy at all,
I can just Heal it away.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:05.380
I see you're wearing your hair ornament.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:12.260
O-Oh, yes, I thought it'd be best to
keep my hair out of the way, and...

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.640
I'm not sure you've noticed,

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:18.470
but that ornament is enchanted.

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:23.230
No matter what may come,
it will keep you safe.

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:25.940
I'm glad you're wearing it today.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.450
I, uh, need to go help with dinner!

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:53.380
<i>Fire Lance</i>!

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:05.940
Wouldn't you say having the Grand Magus
with us is a bit overkill?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:09.650
We simply couldn't let
anything happen to you.

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:13.780
I just assumed he came with
our group to study m--

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.200
Are you all right?

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.540
Y-Yes, thank you!

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:20.740
<i>Wind Blade</i>!

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.380
Are you all right?

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.670
Y-Yes, thank you.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.760
They're much weaker than expected.
There also seem to be fewer of them about.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.130
You're right.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:39.680
We've come quite far into the woods and
have yet to encounter any larger beasts.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:41.010
How odd.

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:46.900
I get it now.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:49.230
No use in stopping simply to wonder.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:52.780
If we're to find answers, we'll need
to proceed further into the woods.

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:53.940
Right!

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.710
The air's so heavy...

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:15.630
Likely because the miasma
is growing denser.

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:17.590
Miasma? <i>This </i>is miasma?

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:40.240
What <i>is </i>that?

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:41.950
If only I knew.

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:48.460
If that horde spots us, we probably
won't make it out of here alive...

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:58.880
<i>Reflection</i>!

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:05.640
Wonderful timing!
You've got a knack for this!

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:08.980
Th-Thank you, Ser! But isn't that a...

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:10.400
Yes,

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:12.360
a salamander.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.440
No...

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:22.070
Here they come!

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:23.780
From both sides?!

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:26.750
Things are getting quite interesting.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:28.000
<i>Fire Lance</i>!

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:33.460
<i>Ground Spear</i>!

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:56.400
They're incredible...

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:59.110
I have to do what I can to help!

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:21.680
Heal!

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:24.850
There's no end to them! We're doomed!

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:27.510
But the Commander's the only one
who can take on that salamander!

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:29.930
They just keep crawling up
out of the swamp!

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:33.900
If we can keep the salamander focused
on Commander Drewes, then maybe...

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.020
Sei!

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:56.920
Are you all right?

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.670
I-I'm fine.

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:01.880
We're not through yet.
Keep your legs steady.

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:02.880
Commander!

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:21.030
He can't.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:23.360
No. No!

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:27.570
Stop!

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:54.980
Sei...

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Next Time

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Saint
